cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "P-RIncHUSP: Parallel Regular Incremental High-Utility Sequential Pattern Mining"
abstract: >
  A Java implementation of P-RIncHUSP, a parallel, incremental framework for
  mining Regular High-Utility Sequential Patterns from a growing quantitative
  sequence database. Regularity is a declared per-dataset constant B: a pattern
  is regular when it recurs at least every B sequences, at every point in time,
  so no bound drifts as the database grows and full-strength pruning stays sound
  in every phase; the relative formulation inherited from the sequential line of
  work is kept for comparison. The incremental result is exact, equal to a full
  re-mine, through sound seed pruning plus a discovery phase over the increment,
  with the seed-split factor fixed by a partition lemma rather than tuned. The
  implementation parallelizes enumeration over prefix subtrees, maintains
  patterns content-driven across batches, computes exact max-measure utility via
  multi-position vertical utility lists, and records per-phase memory, precision
  and the declared bound in every result row.
